{"explanation":"A radian measures an angle by comparing the length of its arc to the circle’s radius: θ = s/r. One radian is the angle that cuts off an arc exactly one radius long. Drag the slider to see how the arc length changes with the angle.","manimCode":"const cx = -2;
const cy = -0.3;
const r = 2.1;
let theta = 1;
const center = [cx, cy, 0];
